            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for an elevator, then the Telugu for to stay overnight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: సర్దుకో",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సర్దుకో — sardukō — \"to settle in; to make do\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "కొత్త గదిలో రెండు రోజుల్లో సర్దుకున్నాను. kotta gadilō reṇḍu rōjullō sardukunnānu. I settled into the new room in two days."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): సర్దుకున్నాను, sardukunnānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సర్దు, to arrange, + -కో: to arrange things for oneself, to make do with what there is."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సర్దుకో (sardukō) is built on సర్దు, \"to arrange, to tidy\", whose origin is not settled, with the ending -కో, \"for oneself\", from కొను, \"to take\" (DEDR 2151)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
